From 18877042c619f9532053e7443b082c81c90adb4e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:56:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(quota): an auth-benched OAuth account is not
 quota evidence; release false episode walls

quota_unavailable() skipped every auth/refresh-benched entry and judged the pool
from the rest, so three healthy anthropic accounts 401-benched for minutes made the
four walled accounts look like the whole pool: workers exited with
SubscriptionQuotaUnavailable resetting days away (worker-3, 2026-11-12 11:32) and
their quota episodes held the cards until then.

- quota_unavailable: a live entry on a non-quota bench without its own model
  cooldown means the pool is not proven exhausted (None); an auth-benched entry
  with a model cooldown still counts by that cooldown. Dead entries and entitlement
  benches stay excluded. live_quota_wall and cron's pool_serving get this for free.
- kanban_quota_episode._outstanding drops a hinted episode wall the live OAuth pool
  now disproves (serves the model, any model for a class route) while no
  provider-wide wall stands, so episodes recorded from the false wall release.
